{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>For the tithe, etc. — therefore, etc.</b> And above it says <b>And to the children of Levi I have given every tithe in Israel</b>, etc., <b>in exchange for their service</b>. It appears that this gift of tithe that HaShem gave to the Levites contains two things: first, the portion pertaining to them in the land, and second, that they do not toil in the land to perform the seven labors required until the grain is kneaded. Therefore the verse states two things: in exchange for their portion in the land and in exchange for their service — Israel stand and do their work so that they [the Levites] may be free for the service of the Tent of Meeting. And note that concerning the Levites He did not say ״I am your portion,״ etc., for the Levites do not merit the portion of HaShem, and therefore they too give the portion of HaShem — terumat ma'aser — from the tithe. And they and their tithe are nothing but the hire of ordinary laborers to minister to the holy one, who is the priest, and to the Tent of Meeting."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:54.049528818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}